.TH convertfonts 1 "June 2026"
.SH NAME
convertfonts \- convert XLFD font names in a Window Maker style file to fontconfig format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B convertfonts
.RI [ options ]
.I stylefile
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B convertfonts
reads the property-list style file
.I stylefile
and rewrites it in place, converting any X Logical Font Description (XLFD)
font names found in the standard font keys
.RI ( IconTitleFont ", " ClipTitleFont ", " LargeDisplayFont ,
.IR MenuTextFont ", " MenuTitleFont ", " WindowTitleFont ,
.IR SystemFont ", " BoldSystemFont )
into the fontconfig pattern syntax used by current Window Maker.
Keys that are already in fontconfig format are left unchanged.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
print a help message with the list of options.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-xlfd
preserve the original XLFD by appending an
.B :xlfd=\fI<xlfd>\fR
hint to the converted font name.
This property is not used by the fontconfig matching engine to find the
font, but it is useful as a hint about what the original font was, to
allow hand-tuning the result or restoring the XLFD.
The default is to omit it, as it results in long and confusing names.
.TP
.B \-\-version
print the version of Window Maker from which the program comes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
when
.I stylefile
was successfully read, converted and written back.
.TP
.B 1
if
.I stylefile
does not exist, is not a regular file, is not a well-formed style
property list, or could not be written, or if the program was not
invoked properly.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR getstyle (1),
.BR setstyle (1),
.BR wmaker (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Window Maker was written by Alfredo K. Kojima <kojima@windowmaker.info>.
convertfonts is part of Window Maker.
